WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.450
A seaside town keeps
two records every day:

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:08.430
ice creams sold, and sunburn cases
treated at its first-aid post.

3
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:11.420
Plot each day as a cross on a graph.

4
00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:13.600
The crosses climb together.

5
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:17.080
A headline asks: is ice cream burning us?

6
00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.800
When two things rise together,
does one cause the other?

7
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:23.210
And would a stronger pattern prove it?

8
00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:25.650
In this mission, you'll
read scatter graphs,

9
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.430
which plot pairs of data as crosses.

10
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:31.580
You'll name the correlation:
positive, negative,

11
00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:34.270
or none at all when
there's no clear pattern.

12
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:37.880
And you'll ask a big question:
when a pattern appears,

13
00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:40.810
does it mean one thing
makes the other happen?

14
00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:44.590
Your mission: decide whether
ice cream causes sunburn.
